/id #edb/ref 17592186413899} {:answer/id #uuid "933dcfb3-eeac-52d0-a670-490f204dfbaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5886a791-872b-5512-8d4a-7f36984d7c4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{k+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413888} :answer-field/id #uuid "af57bbd4-ef11-5f85-bb4a-30a4c400fc40" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413938} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d2077da-26c1-555b-9de1-664d038f0985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413881} {:answer/id #uuid "4e640d6a-beb2-57b7-a9dd-f43c687eb7a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413884} {:answer/id #uuid "995f794b-272c-59bb-9805-fe0d8c3871e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "995f794b-272c-59bb-9805-fe0d8c3871e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413907} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1548cca-677e-55ab-bc20-829c61ca0824" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413939} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16d38fae-3ad8-5767-b6cc-27f8394c79cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k+1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413875} {:answer/id #uuid "5ad8b88d-ebe5-5a30-8319-93038a4adb52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413890} {:answer/id #uuid "9b437258-94d1-561a-b102-aa322807f85f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k+3)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413909} {:answer/id #uuid "fc039b2f-e6d6-5c3d-9036-d08852d95eb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k+2)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b437258-94d1-561a-b102-aa322807f85f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k+3)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413909} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed91eb62-e8ec-58ab-9337-4eba0967376e" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26d461a4-4d45-54f1-9397-8e13a8aa54ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-183365" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to prove the following statement using mathematical induction:\n\n$(n+2)^{2}\\le {3}^{n+1}$ for all $n\\ge 1$\n\nA proof template is outlined below. Fill in the missing statements." :question/worked-solution "To prove a statement using induction, we use the following framework:\n\n- **Step1**: Base Case\n\n- **Step 2**: Inductive Hypothesis\n\n- **Step 3**: Inductive Step\n\n- **Step 4**: Conclusion\n\nIn this case, the general statement $P(n)$ we're required to prove is the following:\n\n$$\n(n+2)^{2}\\le {3}^{n+1}\n$$\n\nWe start by proving the so-called **base case**, $P(1).$ To do this, we substitute $n=1$ into both the left-hand side and right-hand side.\n\nIn our case, this gives the following:\n\n**Base Case**: We first prove that our statement is true for the base case $n=1.$\n\n$$\n(1+2)^{2}\\le {3}^{1+1}\n$$\n\nProving that the base case is true is usually straightforward. We simply calculate the left-hand and right-hand sides independently and show they're equal.\n\nNext, we write down our **inductive hypothesis**. We assume that $P(k)$ is true for some $n=k\\ge 1.$ To do this, we simply replace $n$ with $k$ in our original statement $P(n).$\n\nIn our case, this gives the following:\n\n**Inductive Hypothesis**: We assume that for some $n=k\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n(k+2)^{2}\\le {3}^{k+1}\n$$\n\nThen, we move on to the **inductive step**: We must show that $P(k)⇒P(k+1).$ We start by writing down $P(k+1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}((k+1)+2)^{2} & \\le {3}^{(k+1)+1} \\\\ (k+3)^{2} & \\le {3}^{k+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives:\n\n**Inductive Step**: We're required to prove that\n\n$$\n(k+3)^{2}\\le {3}^{k+2}.\n$$\n\nThe inductive step is where most of the work lies. The idea is to rewrite the left-hand side of this inequality using the inductive hypothesis and apply algebraic techniques to show that this is less than or equal to the right-hand side.\n\nOnce we've shown that $P(k)⇒P(k+1),$ the proof is complete, and we state our **conclusion**.\n\n**Conclusion**: Therefore, $(n+2)^{2}\\le {3}^{n+1}$ for all $n\\ge 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092189 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e61d3403-80d9-5633-b579-dcf452dbc265" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Proof Template"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "086469b0-50ff-592d-907c-51a0b13d0499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413872} {:answer/id #uuid "b6ddea05-7746-515f-b8aa-b091bae2ef2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+{2}^{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413914} {:answer/id #uuid "bae5a540-1a9e-503e-8aae-363834bc24c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+{2}^{k+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413917} {:answer/id #uuid "f8faf1d4-2303-5a10-8a37-a1a5a7b